# 𝚅𝚒𝚋𝚎𝚌𝚛𝚊𝚏𝚝𝚎𝚍. with AI Agents by Vetcoders (c)2024-2026 LibraxisAI
#
# Screenscribe Cloud edge. Caddy terminates TLS (automatic ACME certificates,
# HTTP->HTTPS redirect, HTTP/3) and proxies everything to the `web` service,
# which trusts the X-Forwarded-* headers Caddy sets.
#
# Environment (provided by deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml):
#   SCREENSCRIBE_DOMAIN  public hostname, e.g. cloud.example.com (required)
#   ACME_EMAIL           ACME account contact (compose supplies a fallback)
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here on purpose: the application sets a per-route
# CSP (portal pages, hosted review player, JSON API). An edge-wide policy would
# be too loose for the API or break the review player.
#
# Access logging stays off (Caddy's default). Hosted review URLs (/r/<share_id>)
# are capability links and device-flow URLs carry user codes; neither belongs in
# proxy logs. The application logs requests itself.

{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}

	servers {
		# No read_body and no write timeout: multi-GB uploads, long SSE streams
		# and video playback are legitimately long-lived. Header reads stay tight.
		timeouts {
			read_header 30s
			idle 5m
		}
	}
}

{$SCREENSCRIBE_DOMAIN} {
	# Outer body cap. The largest legitimate body is a review publish: source
	# video (SCREENSCRIBE_CLOUD_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES, default 2 GiB) plus the review
	# bundle (SCREENSCRIBE_CLOUD_MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES, default 512 MiB) plus multipart
	# overhead. The application enforces the exact per-route limits and returns
	# its own 413; keep this value a little above their sum.
	request_body {
		max_size 2600MiB
	}

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		# Default only: a stricter per-route policy from the app wins.
		?Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
		-Via
	}

	# Compress everything except SSE and video. Caddy's default response
	# matcher already limits encoding to compressible types (text/*, JSON,
	# JS, SVG, ...), but text/event-stream is text/* too, and video Range
	# responses must pass byte-exact. The request matcher keeps both out.
	@compressible {
		not path /api/v1/jobs/*/events
		not path /r/*/api/agent/chat/stream
		not path /r/*/video /api/v1/reviews/*/video
		not header Accept *text/event-stream*
	}
	encode @compressible zstd gzip

	# Stripe webhooks (/api/v1/billing/stripe/webhook) pass through untouched:
	# no auth at the edge and no request rewriting, because the app verifies
	# the Stripe-Signature HMAC over the raw body.
	reverse_proxy web:8080 {
		# Flush every write immediately: SSE job progress must not be buffered.
		flush_interval -1

		# Ride out short web restarts (upgrades) instead of returning 502.
		lb_try_duration 15s
		lb_try_interval 250ms

		transport http {
			dial_timeout 5s
			# Per-read/per-write idle limits, not total durations: a 2 GiB upload
			# or an hour of video streams fine as long as bytes keep moving.
			read_timeout 15m
			write_timeout 15m
			# Time from fully sent request (incl. upload body) to response headers.
			response_header_timeout 10m
			keepalive 2m
		}
	}
}
